    "text": "This solution has not been compiled or run, and I did not check it against the example. It is a simple greedy that avoids every conflict rule, so its output should always be valid, but it is not optimised for score.\n\n- **No moves.** Services stay in their initial binaries, so each binary's size never changes.\n- **One owner per binary.** Binary `j` is owned by engineer `j % G`, so no two engineers ever work on the same binary. That keeps `C = 0` and removes any same-binary or same-feature conflicts.\n- **Job cost.** Implementing feature `f` in binary `j` takes `D_f + R_j` days. Each engineer runs their jobs back to back.\n- **Feature order.** Features are sorted by `U / total cost`, descending, where total cost is the sum of `D_f + R_j` over the binaries the feature touches.\n- **Commit rule.** A feature is accepted only if every one of its binaries would finish before day `L`. Features that would miss the limit are skipped without scheduling anything.\n- **Output.** Only engineers with at least one task are listed. Every task takes at least one day and ends before `L`, so no engineer exceeds `L` tasks.\n\n```cpp\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\nint main(){\n    int L,G,S,B,F,N;\n    scanf(\"%d %d %d %d %d %d\",&L,&G,&S,&B,&F,&N);\n    unordered_map<string,int> id;\n    vector<int> bin(S);\n    vector<int> R(B,0);\n    char buf[64];\n    for(int i=0;i<S;i++){\n        int b;\n        scanf(\"%s %d\",buf,&b);\n        id[buf]=i;bin[i]=b;R[b]++;\n    }\n    vector<string> fname(F);\n    vector<int> D(F),U(F);\n    vector<vector<int>> fb(F);\n    vector<double> key(F);\n    for(int i=0;i<F;i++){\n        int m;\n        scanf(\"%s %d %d %d\",buf,&m,&D[i],&U[i]);\n        fname[i]=buf;\n        for(int k=0;k<m;k++){\n            scanf(\"%s\",buf);\n            fb[i].push_back(bin[id[buf]]);\n        }\n        sort(fb[i].begin(),fb[i].end());\n        fb[i].erase(unique(fb[i].begin(),fb[i].end()),fb[i].end());\n        double c=0;\n        for(int b:fb[i])c+=D[i]+R[b];\n        key[i]=U[i]/c;\n    }\n    vector<int> ord(F);\n    iota(ord.begin(),ord.end(),0);\n    stable_sort(ord.begin(),ord.end(),[&](int a,int b){return key[a]>key[b];});\n    vector<long long> tm(G,0);\n    vector<vector<pair<int,int>>> q(G);\n    for(int f:ord){\n        // tentative\n        map<int,long long> tmp;\n        bool ok=true;\n        for(int b:fb[f]){\n            int e=b%G;\n            long long &t=tmp[e];\n            if(t==0)t=tm[e];\n            t+=D[f]+R[b];\n            if(t>=L){ok=false;break;}\n        }\n        if(!ok)continue;\n        for(int b:fb[f]){\n            int e=b%G;\n            tm[e]+=D[f]+R[b];\n            q[e].push_back({f,b});\n        }\n    }\n    int E=0;\n    for(int e=0;e<G;e++)if(!q[e].empty())E++;\n    printf(\"%d\\n\",E);\n    for(int e=0;e<G;e++){\n        if(q[e].empty())continue;\n        printf(\"%d\\n\",(int)q[e].size());\n        for(auto&p:q[e])printf(\"impl %s %d\\n\",fname[p.first].c_str(),p.second);\n    }\n}\n```",
